  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 120 PM EDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nVisible satellite shows very clearly the dividing line being \nrepresented by an are of stratus/stratocu from E IA into SW IL and \nto central KY. The muggy 70+ dewpoints are to the west of this and \n60s (eventually some 50) dewpoints to the northeast. With time, this \nhigher moisture and temperatures will work back, arriving Tuesday \nand Wednesday in response to a northern US disturbance set to \nflatten the upper low and allow a warm front to surge back north. \nDewpoints should return back into the 60s with some med range models \nsuggesting some 70s as well. This combined with a weak cold front \nexpected to pass through Wed into Wed night will bring a chance for \nshowers and thunderstorms to the area. Some finer details still need \nto be worked out regarding coverage, intensity and timing. Model \nblends have been rather conservative in past days, but have began to \nintroduce likely (60 to 70%) pops with decaying precip Wed morning \nNW and renewed development SE in the afternoon/evening. \n\nIn the wake of this wave, temperatures and humidity levels should \nfall once again as we await the next wave towards the weekend, which \nright now looks to remain mainly NW of the area. Lower pops exist in \nthis time frame for the time being.",
